WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:01.359
Let's start with how almost everybody in

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.600
Afghanistan, 95%,

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:05.519
don't have enough food to eat. More than

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:09.520
half the population are at risk of

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:11.600
starvation—that's 23 million people—and it

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.799
includes 3 million children under

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.799
the age of 5.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.439
Poverty, hunger and tough winters are

00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:39.600
nothing new in Afghanistan.

00:01:37.439 --> 00:01:42.720
But right now two things are making the

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:45.759
food crisis so much worse. First, there's

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.759
a terrible drought.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.920
And second, there's the state of the

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.200
economy. 

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.479
So what happened was when the

00:01:59.759 --> 00:02:04.399
Taliban took over, the U.S. froze more

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:06.799
than $9 billion

00:02:04.399 --> 00:02:09.280
of Afghan assets—that's basically money

00:02:06.799 --> 00:02:12.000
and investments held in the U.S.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:14.959
At the same time foreign financial aid

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.720
was also cut pretty much overnight.

00:02:14.959 --> 00:02:20.160
Now you have to realise that under the

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:22.560
old government 75% of its budget was

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.879
foreign aid. And that money's just not

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.959
there anymore. 

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.080
So the U.S. and others don't want the

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.360
Taliban to get their hands on any of

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:59.519
this money. But it's crippled the economy.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.159
One of the big problems is a major

00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:04.800
shortage of cash in a country that runs

00:03:02.159 --> 00:03:07.040
on cash. The banks don't have enough and

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.440
have set limits on withdrawals.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.680
And everything's getting more expensive,

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:14.239
especially imports like fuel, because the

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.560
currency, the afghani, has dropped to an

00:03:14.239 --> 00:03:18.239
all-time low against the dollar.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:22.720
From civil servants to construction

00:03:18.239 --> 00:03:22.720
workers, people just aren't getting paid.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.799
Not a single country has

00:03:48.879 --> 00:03:53.439
officially recognised the Taliban

00:03:50.799 --> 00:03:56.400
government, but the Afghan people are

00:03:53.439 --> 00:03:58.879
also hurting from this isolation. The U.N.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:01.120
and other international aid agencies are

00:03:58.879 --> 00:04:03.760
still working in Afghanistan to deliver

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:05.599
food and supplies. That's the main way

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:08.480
help is getting to the Afghan people

00:04:05.599 --> 00:04:11.200
right now. But Afghanistan needs so much

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:13.599
more than just emergency aid. It needs to

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:15.040
be able to trade like any other country.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.800
So, who are the leaders? Well, they've named

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:33.040
an interim government made up entirely

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:34.880
of senior Taliban members. 

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:37.840
Muhammad Hasan Akhund—he's the acting prime

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:40.160
minister and is on a U.N. sanctions list.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:42.320
Sirajuddin Haqqani, who's designated a

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:44.880
terrorist by the U.S., is the interior

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:46.880
minister. And Muhammad Yaqoob, the son of

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.199
the Taliban's founder, is the defence

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:52.320
minister. There's also the Taliban's

00:04:49.199 --> 00:04:54.400
supreme leader, Hibatullah Akhundzada, who has

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:56.560
ultimate authority over the group. But

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:58.479
he's rarely seen in public.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:01.360
So who's really in charge, and what their

00:04:58.479 --> 00:05:03.440
plans are—it's just not very clear. 

00:05:23.199 --> 00:05:27.280
And there's also

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:29.199
confusion about what the new social

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:31.120
codes are, which so many people were

00:05:29.199 --> 00:05:32.000
worried about when the Taliban came to

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.759
power.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:36.080
The leadership have said that people's

00:05:33.759 --> 00:05:38.720
rights will be protected in accordance

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:41.199
with Islamic law—at least their version

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:44.639
of it. 

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:00.479
The problem is they haven't really specified

00:05:58.319 --> 00:06:02.160
what they mean by that. All we know is

00:06:00.479 --> 00:06:04.000
what's happening on the ground. And

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.240
what's happening on the ground is a

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.479
mixed picture. 

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:43.759
In Herat, Taliban

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:46.080
officials killed four alleged kidnappers

00:06:43.759 --> 00:06:48.400
and hung their bodies up in public. And

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:51.520
in Kabul, two journalists were beaten

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:54.000
when covering protests led by women.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:56.240
And what about the situation for women?

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.160
Well, there have definitely been changes.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:07:00.240
The Women's Affairs Ministry is now the

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:03.039
Ministry for Propagation of Virtue and

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:04.560
Prevention  of Vice. Female aid workers

00:07:03.039 --> 00:07:07.360
have been restricted from doing their

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:09.840
jobs in more than 30 provinces.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:12.080
Women are mostly back at university, but

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:13.840
they have to study separately from men.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:35.280
And there are even fewer answers for

00:07:32.639 --> 00:07:37.440
teenage girls. In most provinces they

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:39.759
haven't been allowed to return to school.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:42.910
The Taliban say that's temporary, but

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:46.560
there's scepticism.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:11.919
OK, so what about security? Because

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:13.919
that's something the Taliban said they

00:08:11.919 --> 00:08:15.759
can handle. 

00:08:21.759 --> 00:08:25.680
But they haven't quite been able to deliver

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:28.639
on that because an affiliate of ISIL—a

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:31.759
group known as ISKP—has stepped up

00:08:28.639 --> 00:08:33.519
attacks since the Taliban took over.

00:08:31.759 --> 00:08:35.279
There was a suicide bombing at Kabul's

00:08:33.519 --> 00:08:38.240
international airport that killed more

00:08:35.279 --> 00:08:41.120
than 180 people. Another attack at a

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:43.599
military hospital killed 25.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:46.080
And ISKP have claimed responsibility for

00:08:43.599 --> 00:08:49.279
at least two attacks on Shia mosques

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:49.279
where dozens were killed.

00:08:49.519 --> 00:08:53.279
Now remember, it wasn't very long ago

00:08:51.519 --> 00:08:54.399
that the Taliban were the ones carrying

00:08:53.279 --> 00:08:56.240
out attacks.

00:08:54.399 --> 00:08:58.480
So one of the big challenges for the new

00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:00.880
government is how to navigate this kind

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:02.320
of role reversal. 

00:09:21.279 --> 00:09:27.839
The Taliban, though, say it's still

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:30.000
early days. 

00:09:31.839 --> 00:09:37.040
Thing is, right now Afghans don't have

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:38.640
time. Their lives are at stake and after

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:41.040
100 days with the Taliban in

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:43.360
charge, there are still so many questions

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:45.600
about Afghanistan's future. Questions

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:47.519
that the Taliban need to answer, but

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:49.680
plenty of others that the U.S. and the

00:09:47.519 --> 00:09:51.760
international community need to answer,

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:53.120
too.

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:55.279
If you want to know more about how

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:57.680
Afghanistan got here, you can watch our

00:09:55.279 --> 00:10:00.000
episode on how the Taliban took Kabul

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:01.519
right here. Also make sure to subscribe

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.240
to this YouTube channel so you don't

00:10:01.519 --> 00:10:05.240
miss our next episode

